{
  /* The web host's hosting Worker — `infrastructure/app-worker/`, the third Cloudflare Worker
     here. Every compiler option below is `infrastructure/relay/tsconfig.json`'s byte for byte,
     and that file carries the argument for why a Worker gets a program of its own:
     `@cloudflare/workers-types` declares `Request`, `Response` and some four hundred other
     globals, and the app under `packages/ui/` must see the DOM's versions of those names and
     nothing else.

     A third file rather than a wider `include` in either of the other two, for
     `infrastructure/share-worker/tsconfig.json`'s reason: `mtg-grimoire-app` is a deploy of its
     own, and one program spanning two Workers lets an edit to one fail the other's check.

     **One file of the shared UI is in this program, by import and not by name**:
     `packages/ui/lib/core/web/assets.ts`, whose `isNavigation` the Worker answers a navigation
     by — the rule the dev server and the preview serve by, shared so the three cannot disagree.
     It is followed from `infrastructure/app-worker/src/index.ts` and so checked a third time,
     under a third set of globals, which is the point: it may name nothing only one runtime has.

     `infrastructure/app-worker/src`'s `*.test.ts` are inside the program, as the relay's are: a
     test that does not type-check can drift from what it asserts about.
     `infrastructure/app-worker/src/vite.d.ts` declares the two Vite imports the fence reads the
     configuration and the Rust sources by, for `infrastructure/relay/src/raw.d.ts`'s reason —
     `vite/client` stays out of a Worker's `types`. */
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    /* No `DOM`: this is not a browser. */
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "types": ["@cloudflare/workers-types"],

    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
